// Title: a decimal of scale 0 prints "plainly" with a trailing '.', a float without one
// Command: timeout -s KILL 5 graphix --no-cache tests-types-decimal-plain-print.gx
// CLAUDE.md: a cast prints a number plainly ("42"). fmt_naked (netidx-value print.rs) prints f64 5.0 as "5"
// but routes a decimal through DecimalFmt, which appends the literal syntax's '.'.
// Observed: ("12345678901234567890.", "12345678901234567890.", "5", "5")
{
  let e = cast<decimal>("12345678901234567890")$;
  (cast<string>(e), "[e]", cast<string>(f64:5.0), "[f64:5.0]")
}
